[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/comments/6515128931","html_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/622#issuecomment-6515128931","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/622","id":6515128931,"node_id":"IC_kwDOU-xXos8AAAABhFT6Yw","user":{"login":"handmade0octopus","id":19230427,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjMwNDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19230427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus","html_url":"https://github.com/handmade0octopus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-30T04:40:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T04:40:20Z","body":"I ported `aed24df` forward onto v1.1.39 (preserving its `SamplerParams`, `drafts_q`, `markov_q8`, prompt lookup and DraftCost paths) and tested it on an RTX 4090 D.\n\n**Correctness passed.** I added a test-only same-state check that runs eager and lazy drafting from the identical model state in each round, then requires the lazy drafts/confidences to be bit-identical and contain every draft the fixed cut keeps. A full 32,768-token prompt + 2,048-token decode completed with **zero mismatches**.\n\n**Performance regressed on the newer 8-row GGUF head.** Over 200 of those same-state rounds:\n\n- eager: **775.7 ms** total drafter time;\n- lazy: **1,813.0 ms** (**2.34x**).\n\nMy working explanation is that v1.1.39's `head_cols_gguf = 8` already lets the whole 5-row block use one head pass, while the `0 -> 2 -> rest` lazy schedule splits it into two passes and adds host synchronizations. This is not a rejection of the PR's measurements on its original hardware/base, but the staging likely needs another look before making it default-on after #639. I have kept it opt-in locally for now. The same-state checker is available if it would be useful for validating a revised schedule.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/comments/6515128931/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/comments/6515208939","html_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/622#issuecomment-6515208939","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/622","id":6515208939,"node_id":"IC_kwDOU-xXos8AAAABhFYy6w","user":{"login":"handmade0octopus","id":19230427,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjMwNDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19230427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus","html_url":"https://github.com/handmade0octopus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/handmade0octopus/repos","events